.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RSA_GENERATE_KEY 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_RSA_gen ,
.Nm RSA_generate_key_ex ,
.Nm RSA_generate_key ,
.Nm RSA_generate_multi_prime_key
.Nd generate RSA key pair
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rsa.h
.Ft EVP_PKEY *
.Fo EVP_RSA_gen
.Fa "unsigned int bits"
.Fc
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_generate_key_ex
.Fa "RSA *rsa"
.Fa "int bits"
.Fa "BIGNUM *e"
.Fa "BN_GENCB *cb"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RSA_generate_multi_prime_key
.Fa "RSA *rsa"
.Fa "int bits"
.Fa "int primes"
.Fa "BIGNUM *e"
.Fa "BN_GENCB *cb"
.Fc
.Pp
The following function has been deprecated since OpenSSL 0.9.8, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft RSA *
.Fo RSA_generate_key
.Fa "int bits"
.Fa "unsigned long e"
.Fa "void (*callback)(int"
.Fa int
.Fa "void *)"
.Fa "void *cb_arg"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn EVP_RSA_gen
generates a new RSA key pair with modulus size
.Fa bits .
.Pp
All of the functions described below are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Fn EVP_RSA_gen ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_Q_keygen 3 ,
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_keygen_init 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_keygen 3 .
.Pp
.Fn RSA_generate_key_ex
generates a 2-prime RSA key pair and stores it in the
.Vt RSA
structure provided in
.Fa rsa .
.Pp
.Fn RSA_generate_multi_prime_key
generates a multi-prime RSA key pair and stores it in the
.Vt RSA
structure provided in
.Fa rsa .
The number of primes is given by the
.Fa primes
parameter.
If the automatic seeding or reseeding of the OpenSSL CSPRNG fails due to
external circumstances (see
.Xr RAND 7 Ns ),
the operation will fail.
.Pp
The modulus size will be of length
.Fa bits ,
the number of primes to form the modulus will be
.Fa primes ,
and the public exponent will be
.Fa e .
Key sizes with
.Em num
\(la 1024 should be considered insecure.
The exponent is an odd number, typically 3, 17 or 65537.
.Pp
In order to maintain adequate security level, the maximum number of
permitted
.Fa primes
depends on modulus bit length:
.Bd -literal
   <1024 | >=1024 | >=4096 | >=8192
   ------+--------+--------+-------
     2   |   3    |   4    |   5
.Ed
.Pp
A callback function may be used to provide feedback about the progress
of the key generation.
If
.Fa cb
is not NULL, it will be called as follows using the
.Xr BN_GENCB_call 3
function described on the
.Xr BN_generate_prime 3
page.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_generate_key
is similar to
.Fn RSA_generate_key_ex
but expects an old-style callback function; see
.Xr BN_generate_prime 3
for information on the old-style callback.
.Bl -bullet
.It
While a random prime number is generated, it is called as described in
.Xr BN_generate_prime 3 .
.It
When the n-th randomly generated prime is rejected as not suitable for
the key,
.Em BN_GENCB_call(cb, 2, n)
is called.
.It
When a random p has been found with p-1 relatively prime to
.Fa e ,
it is called as
.Em BN_GENCB_call(cb, 3, 0) .
.El
.Pp
The process is then repeated for prime q and other primes (if any) with
.Em BN_GENCB_call(cb, 3, i)
where
.Em i
indicates the i-th prime.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_RSA_gen
returns an
.Vt EVP_PKEY
or NULL on failure.
.Pp
.Fn RSA_generate_multi_prime_key
returns 1 on success or 0 on error.
.Fn RSA_generate_key_ex
returns 1 on success or 0 on error.
The error codes can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
.Pp
.Fn RSA_generate_key
returns a pointer to the RSA structure or NULL if the key generation
fails.
.Sh BUGS
.Em BN_GENCB_call(cb, 2, x)
is used with two different meanings.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_PKEY_Q_keygen 3
.Xr BN_generate_prime 3 ,
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 ,
.Xr RAND_bytes 3 ,
.Xr RAND 7
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn EVP_RSA_gen
was added in OpenSSL 3.0. All other functions described here were
deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0. For replacement see
.Xr EVP_PKEY-RSA 7 .
